    "probe_text": "I've traced the entire pipeline. Here's the full ordered list of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. Every step runs under a single `transaction` governance, so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 a caller without that role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n1. **`checkIdempotency`** (`CheckIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. *Side-effect / branch:* if the key was seen and its owner still exists, it republishes that owner and takes the `replay` branch (responds **200**, no create). Otherwise it publishes the key (possibly absent) as a variable and proceeds.\n\n2. **`validate`** (`ValidateOwnerFields`) \u2014 the **only** step that binds `@RequestBody` (`OwnerFieldsDto`). *Validation:* rejects if any required field is missing/blank \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (satisfied by either structured `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`), `city`, `telephone` \u2014 reporting **all** offenders at once \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`. *Side-effect:* publishes the body for later steps.\n\n3. **`validatePostcode`** (`ValidateOwnerPostcode`) \u2014 *Validation:* if a postcode is supplied, it must be well-formed and in range for the city \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode passes.\n\n4. **`validateRegistrationDate`** (`ValidateRegistrationDate`) \u2014 *Validation:* if a registration date is supplied and is after the server date (`LocalDate.now()`) \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Checked against the raw supplied value, before any defaulting/rolling.\n\n5. **`normalizeTelephone`** (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* rewrites `telephone` to canonical E.164 on the body. *Validation:* a number that can't form valid E.164 \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n6. **`normalizeEmail`** (`NormalizeOwnerEmail`) \u2014 absent/blank email left untouched. *Validation:* a present email must be syntactically valid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException`. *Side-effect:* stores it back lower-cased/normalized.\n\n7. **`rejectDisposableEmail`** (`RejectDisposableEmail`) \u2014 *Validation:* a present, well-formed email whose domain is a known disposable provider \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n8. **`normalizeAddress`** (`NormalizeOwnerAddress`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand street abbreviations) and sets the flat `address` to the composed canonical form.\n\n9. **`ensureUniqueHousehold`** (`EnsureUniqueHousehold`) \u2014 *Validation:* unless the request sets `sharesHousehold`, rejects if the household id (last name + postcode) matches any existing **active** owner \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException`.\n\n10. **`ensureCityCapacity`** (`EnsureCityCapacity`) \u2014 *Validation:* counts existing owners in the city (over `findAll`, case/whitespace-insensitive); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n11. **`build`** (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper` and publishes it.\n\n12. **`assignHousehold`** (`AssignHousehold`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* stamps `householdId` (deterministic from last name + postcode).\n\n13. **`defaultRegistrationDate`** (`DefaultRegistrationDate`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* if no registration date, sets it to `LocalDate.now()`.\n\n14. **`rollRegistrationDate`** (`RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* if the effective date falls on Sat/Sun, rolls it forward to the following Monday (applies to both supplied and defaulted dates).\n\n15. **`ensureDailyLimit`** (`EnsureDailyLimit`) \u2014 *Validation:* counts owners already registered on that (business) day; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 `DailyLimitReachedException`. Uses the rolled date.\n\n16. **`assignCustomerCode`** (`AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash over normalized telephone + last name), de-duplicates against existing active owners' codes with a `-<n>` suffix, and sets `customerCode`.\n\n17. **`countNamesakes`** (`CountNamesakes`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* counts existing active owners matching first + last name and sets `namesakeCount` (pre-create state).\n\n18. **`countHousehold`** (`CountHouseholdMembers`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* counts existing active owners in the same household, plus one for this owner, and sets `householdMemberCount`.\n\n19. **`detectPossibleDuplicate`** (`DetectPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* unless `sharesHousehold`, finds an existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` (flag) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (matched id).\n\n20. **`save`** (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n21. **`recordIdempotency`** (`RecordIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore` (no-op otherwise) so a repeat replays.\n\n22. **`audit`** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* logs to the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n23. **`respond`** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 *Side-effect:* maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (from the day's registration count), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes\n- **Validation order is deliberate**: field presence \u2192 postcode \u2192 future date all run *before* any normalization or entity building, so a bad body is a 400 and doesn't leak into side-effects. Telephone/email normalization can also reject (400) mid-normalization.\n- The four \"reject\" rules that throw are the household-uniqueness, city-capacity, and daily-limit checks, plus the format/domain validators above.\n- Escalation handlers under `officefloor/escalation/` map each exception to its HTTP status (the `*Exception` types here \u2192 400; `HouseholdDuplicate`/`CityAtCapacity`/`DailyLimitReached` have their own handlers)."
